#2# Double Pointer
Problem Statement
Write a C program to declare a double pointer and display the values stored in the variable,
pointer, and double pointer.
Program
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

int main()
{
int num;
int *ptr;
int **dptr;

printf(&quot;Enter an integer: &quot;);
scanf(&quot;%d&quot;, &amp;num);

ptr = &amp;num;
dptr = &amp;ptr;

printf(&quot;\nValue of variable = %d\n&quot;, num);
printf(&quot;Value using pointer = %d\n&quot;, *ptr);
printf(&quot;Value using double pointer = %d\n&quot;, **dptr);

printf(&quot;\nAddress of variable = %p\n&quot;, (void *)&amp;num);
printf(&quot;Address stored in pointer = %p\n&quot;, (void *)ptr);
printf(&quot;Address stored in double pointer = %p\n&quot;, (void *)dptr);

return 0;
}
Output
Enter an integer: 50

Value of variable = 50
Value using pointer = 50
Value using double pointer = 50

Address of variable = 0x7ffd1234
Address stored in pointer = 0x7ffd1234

Address stored in double pointer = 0x7ffd1238
Explanation
 num stores the actual value.
 ptr stores the address of num.
 dptr stores the address of ptr.
 *ptr gives the value of num.
 **dptr also gives the value of num.
